# Shell scripts that run inside a Linux image must keep LF. This repository is
# developed on Windows with core.autocrlf=true, which would check the entrypoint
# out with CRLF; a CRLF `#!/bin/sh` fails in the container with
# "no such file or directory", which reads like a missing file rather than a
# line ending. The Dockerfile strips CR as well, for clones whose git config
# ignores this file.
*.sh text eol=lf
docker/entrypoint.sh text eol=lf
